    "Home",
    "Services",
    "About",
    "How to join",
    "Contact",
    "submit a project",
    "Open Source Europe (OSE) is a European nonprofit that offers open source projects a simple fiscal home : receive donations, manage expenses, and grow — without the burden of creating a legal entity.",
    "submit a project",
    "for funders",
    "Open Source Europe (OSE) is a European nonprofit that offers open source projects a simple fiscal home : receive donations, manage expenses, and grow — without the burden of creating a legal entity.",
    "submit a project",
    "for funders",
    "// Our mission",
    "Our mission is simple: provide open source projects with the legal and financial framework they need to operate like an organization — without becoming one. At OSE, we keep admin invisible and impact visible, so contributors focus on their tools, not their tax status.",
    "Dries Buytaert",
    "Founder of Drupal",
    "// How to join us",
    "Create your collective on Open Collective with a ready legal and financial framework",
    "Start receiving donations and grants from people, companies, or foundations.",
    "Manage expenses openly on our platform, with full compliance and trust",
    "// Key benefits",
    "Radical transparency : every budget is public",
    "Simple admin processes",
    "A nonprofit structure compliant with EU law",
    "Eligibility for both European and US-based funding.",
    "// Supported project",
    "Hundreds of projects already trust OSE to manage their finances transparently. We support everything from small, single-maintainer libraries to large collaborative ecosystems — always without bureaucracy.",
    "explore all on open collective",
    "FM",
    "\"For open source projects, finances can be traumatic. Open Source Europe removes that pain, making expenses, fundraising, and transparency as easy as it could possibly be.\" - Dee, Fedi Monster",
    "view project",
    "Semantic MediaWiki",
    "\"For open source projects, finances can be traumatic. Open Source Europe removes that pain, making expenses, fundraising, and transparency as easy as it could possibly be.\" - Dee, Fedi Monster",
    "view project",
    "Project EdgeTX",
    "ASince 2021, the RC model transmitter firmware project EdgeTX, has chosen OpenCollective to manage its funds. We appreciate the openness of public financial records and the ease of management that Open Collective offers to our open-source project.",
    "view project",
    "// apply project",
    "OSE works with funders, companies, and individual donors who believe that open source deserves lasting support. Their contributions strengthen the ecosystem and help projects of all sizes thrive.",
    "submit a project",
    "// become a funder",
    "OSE offers a trusted, compliant channel for donations and grants in both the EU and the US. Thanks to ED certification, US foundations can give tax-deductible grants.",
    "contact us",
    "// Partners & sponsors",
    "OSE works with funders, companies, and individual donors who believe that open source deserves lasting support. Their contributions strengthen the ecosystem and help projects of all sizes thrive.",
    "// faq",
    "Do I need to create a legal entity?",
    "No. OSE provides the fiscal structure so you don’t have to.",
    "Do you control my project?",
    "No. Your project remains fully autonomous: your project, your rules.",
    "How long does it take to get started?",
    "Most projects are live within a week.",
    "Who can apply?",
    "Any open source project, regardless of size or maturity.",
    "Do we lose independence?",
    "No. Your project remains fully yours: your project, your rules.",
    "Start in minutes. No paperwork. No barriers. Just open source, sustained.",
    "Submit a project",
